 "what": "cost per unit of lam and of arclength (u1, u2, t, lam) of the 50 digit natural continuation (tools/reclose-continue.py) over the SAME stretch of lam as the PeriCont cost of cost-comparison.json (before_creep: accepted steps 1 to 1220 of t35 - and 1 to 623 of t44 -), started from accepted step 1 of the stored trace re-closed in 50 digits (tools/reclose.py), in the direction of the trace (falling lam). Two step sizes in lam per family; \"chosen\" is the run with the largest step at which every step converged. seconds = the sum of the wall seconds of the steps (the re-closing of the start orbit is not in it, as the corrector seconds of PeriCont do not hold the closing of its start); lam_covered = converged steps x |step|; arclength = the sum over the steps of sqrt(du1^2 + du2^2 + dt^2 + dlam^2). The steps are not an optimum search: a larger step may be cheaper still. The last orbit of a run is not checked (no witness). largest_relative_difference_to_the_stored_trace compares u1, u2, t of every step with the stored double precision trace linearly interpolated in lam (limited by the spacing of the stored points, large in the early steps of t44 -).",
